# Kernel compatibility manifest read by guard.sh (halow_guard_check).
#
# Format: one record per line, fields separated by '|'. Blank lines and lines starting with '#'
# are ignored. Any other malformed or incomplete content makes the guard refuse.
#
#   release|<release>|vermagic|<vermagic the bundled and host modules must carry>
#   kernel_build|<release>|uname_v|<kernel build string, as printed by "uname -v">
#   kernel_banner|<release>|<exact text of /proc/version>
#   kernel_config|<release>|<SHA-256 of the decompressed /proc/config.gz text>
#   host_module|<release>|<cfg80211|mac80211|libarc4>|<path under /lib/modules/<release>>|<SHA-256 of the file as stored>|<GNU build-id>
#   artifact|<release>|<bundled module file>|<srcversion of that file, or none>
#
# Every listed release needs exactly one release, kernel_build, kernel_banner and kernel_config
# row, one host_module row for each of cfg80211, mac80211 and libarc4, and artifact rows for
# morse.ko and dot11ah.ko. A release with an incomplete set is refused. A host_module path names
# the exact file including its extension; its hash is of the file as stored (a compressed
# module is hashed compressed).
#
# What the guard can and cannot establish: it identifies the exact official module files of
# the supported release and the running kernel's banner and configuration. It cannot defend
# against a hostile root user on the host or a kernel deliberately forged to mimic these
# strings. Only the release listed here is accepted; a different Home Assistant OS release is
# refused until its values are added.
#
# Why exactly one release is listed: the image bundles ONE flat set of modules (morse.ko and
# dot11ah.ko), built for kernel 6.18.58. A host running any other kernel release could not load
# them (vermagic mismatch), and the guard must not accept a release that the bundled modules
# cannot load. The launch target is the current Home Assistant OS release (18.4); the rows
# for 18.3 (kernel 6.18.52-haos) were therefore removed, not kept alongside. A host on 18.3 is
# refused with the "not supported" message below, before anything on the host is changed.
#
# Where the values come from: the Home Assistant OS 18.4 release for the Home Assistant Green,
# as published on the GitHub release (signature chain not verified), read from two public
# artifacts that agreed on every value (their kernel and root filesystem images are
# byte-identical):
#   haos_green-18.4.img.xz  (disk image, 331564644 bytes)
#     SHA-256 b5d9a4869a9c70a9d87946f8ba90c72b0a42b393404fa8bf82e161452b8c6aba
#   haos_green-18.4.raucb   (update bundle, 206846360 bytes)
#     SHA-256 8e7189352061686fb9c54bacdd6fe8fa700a50ec5af5630df1cf0af39ff25a3f
# Both root filesystems carry each module once, uncompressed and signed with the build's own
# generated key, so the file hashes are unique to the official build:
#   kernel/net/wireless/cfg80211.ko  682489 bytes
#   kernel/net/mac80211/mac80211.ko  956601 bytes
#   kernel/lib/crypto/libarc4.ko       5177 bytes
# The banner, the build string and the configuration hash (276698 bytes of decompressed
# configuration) come from the same release's kernel image. The bundled morse.ko and dot11ah.ko
# rows record those files' own srcversion; both modules were rebuilt for 6.18.58-haos and carry
# its vermagic. None of the host values below has been compared with the modules on a real
# device, and the rebuilt modules have not been loaded on one: unverified.
#
# Earlier versions of this file identified the host modules by per-module source hashes; the
# supported kernel records none, so those rows were removed and replaced by the exact file
# identity above.
#
release|6.18.58-haos|vermagic|6.18.58-haos SMP preempt mod_unload aarch64
